===================================================
Mr.Z QQ Bot — A Group Chat Bot (NoneBot2 + NapCat)
===================================================

A QQ group-chat bot built on **NoneBot2** with the **OneBot v11** adapter and
**NapCat**. Plugin-based architecture with ready-to-use features including
daily greetings, cross-group message forwarding, web/image rendering, web
search, and Minecraft server status queries.

.. contents:: Table of Contents
   :depth: 3

------------
Features
------------

Commands (prefixes are optional, type the name directly):

.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 30 70

   * - Command
     - Description
   * - ``/search <keywords>`` / ``/web``
     - Concurrent multi-backend search (DuckDuckGo / Bing), merged and de-duplicated
   * - ``/jrrp``
     - Daily luck score; deterministically derived from the date + user QQ number,
       so the result is stable for the whole day
   * - ``/alipay <amount>`` / ``/pay``
     - Plays the Alipay "payment received" voice memo. Digits and Chinese amounts
       are both supported (e.g. ``/alipay 114514``)
   * - ``/mc <server address>``
     - Query a Minecraft Java server (online players / latency / MOTD)
   * - ``/mc motd|ping|player|status <address>``
     - Sub-commands of ``/mc`` for a single field
   * - ``text2pic <text>``
     - Render text to an image (Playwright)
   * - ``md2pic``
     - Render ``doc/rule.md`` to an image
   * - ``html2pic <url>``
     - Full-page screenshot of a URL; only the top portion when beyond max height
   * - ``/member update``
     - Manually refresh the current group's member list cache
   * - ``/member show``
     - Show the current group's member list as an image table
   * - ``/sync``
     - Forward new messages from configured source groups to the current group
       as merged forward cards
   * - Poke the bot (group / private)
     - Triggers a server status report (``nonebot-plugin-status``)

Automatic behavior:

* **Daily greetings** — greeting messages at 08:10 / 14:00 / 20:00 to the
  configured groups.
* **Scheduled group sync** — at 09:00 every day, forward new messages from
  source groups to the target groups.
* **Welcome messages** — a random welcome line when someone joins the group.
* **Member tracking** — the member list cache is refreshed on join/leave
  notices.
* **Goodnight replies** — keywords such as "睡觉了 / 碎觉了 / 睡了" get a
  goodnight reply.
* **Blacklist / whitelist** — messages from listed users are silently dropped
  (management is SuperUser-only).

------------
Quick Start
------------

Requirements: Python >= 3.10 (3.12 inside Docker).

Local run
================

.. code-block:: bash

   # 1. Configure environment variables
   cp .env.example .env      # fill in SUPERUSERS / QQ_ACCOUNT, etc.

   # 2. One-command launch (auto-creates .venv and installs deps + Chromium)
   ./start.sh

Docker run
================

.. code-block:: bash

   # 1. Create the NapCat login config
   echo "QQ_ACCOUNT=<bot_qq_uin>" > .env.docker

   # 2. Start (auto-generates NapCat OneBot config and builds the image)
   ./start.sh docker

   # 3. Log in to QQ by scanning the QR code
   #    Open the NapCat WebUI at http://localhost:6099

Other commands:

.. code-block:: bash

   ./start.sh stop        # stop (docker compose down)
   ./start.sh logs        # tail logs (docker compose logs -f)
   ./rebuild-bot.sh       # rebuild and restart the bot service

-------------
Configuration
-------------

All configuration is injected through environment variables; NoneBot2 reads
them automatically as snake_case options. Key variables:

.. code-block:: ini

   HOST=0.0.0.0
   PORT=6060
   LOG_LEVEL=INFO
   SUPERUSERS=["<your_qq_uin>"]        # admin QQ number
   COMMAND_START=["/", ""]            # command prefix ("" = no prefix needed)
   QQ_ACCOUNT=<bot_qq_uin>            # bot QQ number

Daily greeting / group sync:

.. code-block:: ini

   GREETING_TARGETS=["<group_id>"]              # groups that get daily greetings
   FORWARD_SOURCE_GROUPS=["<group_id>"]         # source groups for /sync
   SYNC_TARGET_GROUPS=["<group_id>"]            # scheduled-sync targets (daily 09:00)
   GREETING_TEST_TIME="HH:MM:SS"                # optional, test greeting trigger time

Search backend:

.. code-block:: ini

   WEB_SEARCH_BACKEND=bing,ddg                 # comma-separated, default is all

Tool (read-only) access control:

.. code-block:: ini

   TOOL_ALLOW_DIRS=/home/host,/app/data         # allowed directories
   TOOL_DENY=.ssh,.aws,.env,id_rsa,.pem,...     # forbidden path fragments
   TOOL_MAX_OUT=3000                            # max chars per tool output

Env files:

* ``.env`` — main config (gitignored, see ``.env.example``)
* ``.env.prod`` — production override (gitignored)
* ``.env.docker`` — only ``QQ_ACCOUNT``, used by NapCat to log in

--------------
Project Layout
--------------

.. code-block:: text

   bot.py                      # entry point: init NoneBot2, register OneBot v11
   pyproject.toml              # dependencies + [tool.nonebot] plugin loading
   start.sh                    # one-command start (local / docker / stop / logs)
   docker-compose.yml          # napcat + bot services
   Dockerfile                  # bot image (includes Playwright system deps)
   src/plugins/
     websearch/                # search commands + reusable web_search() library
     htmlrender/               # Playwright renderer (text/markdown/html -> image)
     imagerender/              # text2pic / md2pic / html2pic commands
     namelist/                 # blacklist / whitelist (silent preprocessor drop)
     members/                  # member tracking + /member list rendering
     jrrp/                     # daily luck /jrrp + goodnight keywords
     alipayvoice/              # Alipay voice memo /alipay
     ping/                     # Minecraft server query /mc
     welcome/                  # random welcome messages
     restart/                  # bot restart command
     daily_greeting/           # scheduled daily greetings
     groupforward/             # cross-group merged forward sync
     nonebot-plugin-apscheduler/ # APScheduler integration
     nonebot-plugin-status/    # status / health check
   napcat/                     # NapCat runtime data (gitignored)
   data/                       # runtime data: members, forward anchors, etc. (gitignored)

.. note::

   ``src/plugins/websearch`` doubles as an importable library, so other plugins
   can call ``web_search()`` directly.

-------------------
Docker Architecture
-------------------

``docker-compose.yml`` defines two services:

* **napcat** — the QQ client with a WebUI (``6099`` port) that pushes events
  back to the bot over WebSocket.
* **bot** — the NoneBot2 service on ``6060``, talking to NapCat over
  ``ws://bot:6060/onebot/v11/ws`` on the internal network.

For live reload, the bot container mounts ``./src``, ``./data`` and ``bot.py``.
Optionally, ``HOST_HOME`` mounts a host directory read-only as ``/home/host``
inside the container (the bot's "computer").

Troubleshooting
================

* **Restart only the bot without taking the whole compose down** — run
  ``./rebuild-bot.sh``.
* **Playwright Chromium missing** — run ``playwright install chromium`` locally
  (already bundled in the Docker image).
* **Group sync not working** — make sure ``FORWARD_SOURCE_GROUPS`` and
  ``SYNC_TARGET_GROUPS`` are configured; otherwise the job is never scheduled.

------------
Tech Stack
------------

* NoneBot2 / nonebot-adapter-onebot — bot framework and the OneBot v11 adapter
* NapCat — QQ protocol implementation (deployed via Docker)
* Playwright + Pillow — render web pages, text and Markdown to images
* APScheduler — daily greetings and scheduled sync
* mcstatus — Minecraft server status queries
* httpx — HTTP requests for search

---------------------
License / Maintenance
---------------------

This project evolved from ``smart-driver`` (project description: *Revived from
smart-driver*). There is no built-in test suite or lint configuration; follow
the existing plugin conventions when contributing.
